<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is authoritarian Vietnam ready to phase out the death penalty?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0c939e71f0f8ffbec7f47f7ce174665fb83b60148f7adb32c0d26d5d90bd1b9</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-authoritarian-vietnam-ready-to-phase-out-the-death-penalty/a-80064271--09c5b90052b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-authoritarian-vietnam-ready-to-phase-out-the-death-penalty/a-80064271?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vietnam has voted to abolish the death penalty for six more crimes, continuing a decades-long trend of restricting capital punishment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia trade deal opens new markets, but challenges remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1dc2d7e7304182c9638253e317302822da524cd740d1241e5d70fe82584304dd</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568--6d93bfcf9a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The agreement offers new export and investment opportunities for Jakarta and Brussels. But can Indonesia turn Europe's growing interest in its markets and critical minerals into sustainable gains at home?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Resolve tariff concerns in trade talks — India tells US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9af35e1afaa8ff050ae4ecbfbb8604a038751973f23ce6c1d581eef41058a34c</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-resolve-tariff-concerns-in-trade-talks-india-tells-us/live-80056202--8adafaf8404f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-resolve-tariff-concerns-in-trade-talks-india-tells-us/live-80056202?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India has denied US claims that New Delhi's policies promote excess manufacturing capacity. Further headlines from India include Constitution Day celebrations. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Chinese companies circumvent chips sanctions in Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0936376b57468a71fb9b09975d53478da475e6c607a73c3fe0c1ec50404a0366</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-chinese-companies-circumvent-chips-sanctions-in-southeast-asia/a-80041002--ca78b0ef9d25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-chinese-companies-circumvent-chips-sanctions-in-southeast-asia/a-80041002?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">High-tech AI chips are hard to get in China because of US restrictions. To get around this, Chinese companies often use offshore computing capacity, particularly in Southeast Asia. The US is also trying to stop it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kim Jong Un tours nuclear material sites, urges wider use of tactical nuclear weapons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:623e2bd303617c2c7c6b4ad7e068f1a34e335e5a79a0e6b49bbce744df98ac4a</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T04:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kim-jong-un-tours-nuclear-material-sites-urges-wider-use-of-tactical-nuclear-weapons/a-80055887--3e6bd65b24cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kim-jong-un-tours-nuclear-material-sites-urges-wider-use-of-tactical-nuclear-weapons/a-80055887?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's Kim Jong Un visited sites that produce nuclear material and told his military to focus on tactical weapons, saying his country's nuclear status is irreversible.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Indian nationals are still ending up in Russia's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bae444b74fa5554df4aaff9a26544a7e1ffe1b09f7ce9054ef46d3d17dbf9de0</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537--f2a88cb80a6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Whether through deception or desperation, Indians continue to be drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine. What can New Delhi do to protect its citizens from ending up fighting in Ukraine?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Afghanistan, no female doctor often means no treatment for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ad5167b383f10ee0982bdc083085ecd12441d4d42f8f6136834c29b00e27400</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053--cac71a2a15bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Millions of women in Afghanistan, particularly pregnant women, are suffering under Taliban restrictions and are increasingly losing access to life-saving medical care.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea expels Swiss envoy over sanctions on camp accused of indoctrinating Ukrainian children</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aef453791e7492c03f7f184877cdabeaa3a477dc3f807626a39c534d3815cc4</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expels-swiss-envoy-over-sanctions-on-camp-accused-of-indoctrinating-ukrainian-children/a-80043648--1c076b22f29b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expels-swiss-envoy-over-sanctions-on-camp-accused-of-indoctrinating-ukrainian-children/a-80043648?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea has ordered Switzerland to close its newly reopened diplomatic office. The dispute centers on Swiss sanctions against a camp accused of indoctrinating Ukrainian children from Russian-occupied territories.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Deepfakes and 'US abandons Taiwan' claims spread ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd7b7b86b9591261527ffdf67165ccd4d5fbc97b0f4cd097bd5904a7384c8759</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834--56b12ab42141.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of local elections, Taiwan is seeing a surge in AI-generated attacks on mayoral candidate Puma Shen, alongside disinformation portraying the US as abandoning the island.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: US prepares new tariffs after trade probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83b838f35a03ba6158b654bbbc6562df99ef49b1289f92ade04461a9560c6930</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T04:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-prepares-new-tariffs-after-trade-probe/live-80042306--026b51bba49a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-prepares-new-tariffs-after-trade-probe/live-80042306?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The United States is reportedly readying fresh tariffs on India and 15 other economies under a trade probe. Also, a woman was allegedly gangraped by her colleagues in the national capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China launches Shenzhou-24 to Tiangong station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4643277edf231fae35d0002ba958baa29733e594e9554da5a21b8e839d546dbf</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T02:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-launches-shenzhou-24-to-tiangong-station/a-80042281--a0d093ca339a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-launches-shenzhou-24-to-tiangong-station/a-80042281?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Chinese crew is on its way to the Tiangong station after a launch that China called a complete success. This includes a Pakistani pilot, who is making a brief visit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US jury convicts Huawei of violating sanctions, stealing trade secrets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3be764915ee308b6c591240c2e3d167b4ac5442c67c3cdea4dcfec1195b9dc6</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T02:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-jury-convicts-huawei-of-violating-sanctions-stealing-trade-secrets/a-80042172--af37cbca81fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-jury-convicts-huawei-of-violating-sanctions-stealing-trade-secrets/a-80042172?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Huawei was found guilty of 10 out of 12 charges levelled against it. The company said it plans to appeal the verdict.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5d9b6125e17cd56fed8a63c7ad246e37603a64e80263920b52a1073cd3a2152</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbad263e975361b7896f254012d1320aaf7ca81c01983c492315e060ecb5ce60</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
